From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0273: camera phases 2 and 3 (link, one RAW frame)

Phases 2 and 3 (research/camera.md 5-11), kern.sweet_cam_arg the argument:
op 10 replays the sensor's init, mode and stream-on tables over CCI (HM6
modes 0/1/4, 4H7 mode 0, generated into sweet_cam_tables.h; bursts in 9-byte
pieces, queue 0 in batches of up to 58 words between LOCK and UNLOCK, with a report); op 11 votes the
CSIPHY rails, turns on the PHY/PPI/CSID clocks, programs CSIPHY0 (C-PHY 3
trios) or CSIPHY1 (D-PHY 4 lanes), PPI and CSID0 RDI0 and logs the packet,
ECC, CRC and byte counters and the PHY status; op 12 takes one frame through
TFE0 RDI0 and write master 7 (frame mode) into the pool 0xD7000000 (144 MB)
via an identity SMMU bank for stream 0x400, logging the TFE/bus IRQs,
overflow, size violation, SMMU state and the first bytes; op 13 stops; op 14
pattern-tests the pool. kern.sweet_cam_seek / kern.sweet_cam_frame /
kern.sweet_cam_frame_len give the frame to user space in 1 MB reads.
TopazModem exports smmu_identity() and a write-combined physical mapping.
CCI recovery: a reset also clears the masters' timing registers, so 0272's reset after
a NACK left both masters hung; the global reset now rewrites them, and a NACK or
timeout on a master is recovered the Linux/Android way (HALT_REQ 0x034, the halt
acknowledge, that master's reset 0x3F1/0x3F001, its timings), with the global reset
as the fallback.

